module System/Memory

### Cycle-collector state for the Bacon-Rajan synchronous recycler (see
### internal-wiki/v0.4.x-cycle-collector.md). Touched only by the single-threaded collector.
choice RoamState
    ### In use — not garbage.
    LIVE: 0
    ### Being traced this cycle-collection pass.
    SCANNING: 1
    ### Garbage candidate (provisionally unreachable).
    GARBAGE: 2
    ### Buffered as a possible cycle root.
    SUSPECTED: 3

### Biased reference-counting controller for {Roamed[T]} — the hybrid of {RetainManager[T]}
### (non-atomic, single-thread) and {GuardManager[T, P]} (atomic + lock). Starts in LOCAL mode:
### one non-atomic `count`, no lock, owner only. On the first escape across a concurrency boundary
### `promote()` flips it — irreversibly — to ESCAPED mode: `count` becomes atomic and a reentrant,
### TASK-keyed exclusive lock is armed. The mode flag lives here, at the one address every {Roamed}
### handle shares, so all handles observe the flip.
###
### v1 biased scheme = SINGLE count + one-way flip (the classic dual-counter BRC, which keeps the
### owner fast even AFTER escape, is a deferred perf optimization). Reentrancy is keyed to the
### task/coroutine id (NOT the OS thread) because M:N migration moves a coroutine across workers.
### One controller type serves every entity: what depends on the entity's type is the address of its data and the three
### hooks the creator is given, so the controller's routines are built once, not once per entity type.
entity RoamManager
    ### Reference count. Read/written non-atomically in LOCAL mode, atomically once ESCAPED.
    secret count: U64
    ### EXPERIMENT (object-level liveness): weak/observer count. A weak observer does NOT keep the entity
    ### alive; it keeps the CONTROLLER alive as a tombstone after the entity data is freed, so
    ### `is_destroyed()` can safely answer without dangling. LOCAL-only for now (non-atomic, single-thread);
    ### concurrency hardening (rwlock) is a follow-up.
    secret weak_count: U64
    ### EXPERIMENT (object-level liveness): set once the managed entity's DATA has been freed — via either
    ### free path (RC-drop `unhold` or cycle-collect `cyclic_finalize`). This is the path-agnostic ground
    ### truth for `is_destroyed()`: a CYCLE-collected node's `count` is NOT zero (internal cycle edges keep
    ### it up), so liveness cannot key on the count — it keys on this flag. The controller struct itself
    ### lives on as a tombstone while weak observers remain; only `dead` says the entity is gone.
    ### **`Unbroken[U8]`, not `Bool`** (same reasoning as `escaped`): the free path publishes the flip and
    ### `is_destroyed()`/`is_alive()` read it from any thread — a plaintext `Bool` would be a data race and
    ### could be cached. `0` = live, `1` = dead. (`Bool` also lowers to `i1`, which has no HW atomic.)
    secret dead: Unbroken[U8]
    ### `0` = LOCAL, `1` = ESCAPED. Flipped once by `promote()`. Every handle observes it.
    ### **`Unbroken[U8]`, not `Bool`:** `promote()` publishes the flip cross-thread at the escape site
    ### and non-owner threads read it from `retain`/`release`/`guard_enter` — a plaintext `Bool` would
    ### be a data race (and could be hoisted/cached so a promoted object still looks LOCAL forever).
    ### SeqCst load/store on the atomic gives the release-store / acquire-load the flip needs. `Bool`
    ### also lowers to `i1`, which has no hardware atomic; the flag is `0`/`1` over `Unbroken[U8]`.
    secret escaped: Unbroken[U8]
    ### The address of the managed entity.
    secret data: Addr
    ### Exclusive-lock flag (`0` free / `1` held). Armed and used only in ESCAPED mode.
    secret locked: Unbroken[U8]
    ### Task/coroutine id of the current lock holder (`0` when free). Task-keyed for migration safety.
    secret holder_task: Unbroken[U64]
    ### Reentrancy depth. Only ever touched by the holder under mutual exclusion, so non-atomic.
    secret depth: U64
    ### Cycle-collector state (Bacon-Rajan). Touched only by the single-threaded collector.
    secret state: RoamState
    ### Where this controller sits in the collector's roots buffer, as its index plus one, or `0` when it is not
    ### in the buffer. Dedups `mark_cycle_candidate` and lets a removal skip the search.
    secret buffered_at: U32
    ### Address of the builder-generated per-type trace function for `T` (visits `T`'s `Roamed`
    ### fields). `Addr.hollow()` = no trace wired yet / `T` has no `Roamed` fields (cannot form a cycle).
    ### Called as `fn(controller_address)`; reinterprets and reports each `Roamed` field through `ingrid_cyclic_visit_child`.
    secret trace_hook: Addr
    ### Address of the builder-generated per-type free function for `T`. Called as
    ### `fn(controller_address)` when the collector reaps a GARBAGE node: runs the managed
    ### entity's `destruct` (type-correct) then frees the controller. `Addr.hollow()` until wired.
    secret free_hook: Addr
    ### Address of the managed entity type's own `destruct`, run by the last strong release. Ingrid's Roamed
    ### runtime (`Ingrid/lapila/roam.lpa`) cannot name `T`, so it calls the entity's teardown through this.
    secret drop_hook: Addr
    ### How many `for` loops and in-place element accesses are using the entity's element positions right now
    ### (Mielia's shape use). Every name of the entity shares this controller, so a change made through any of
    ### them sees the use. Kept by the builder through `Roamed.begin_shape_use`/`end_shape_use`.
    secret shape_users: U64
    ### The controller of another entity this one keeps alive (one strong handle to it), or the hollow address. An
    ### emitter adapter keeps the collection it walks this way, wherever the adapter is stored. The last strong
    ### release lets it go.
    secret kept: Addr

### Builder intrinsic: yields a closure over this type's synthesized `roam_trace` cycle-collector
### hook (visits the entity's `Roamed` fields). ExpressionLoweringPass rewrites every call to a
### routine-value reference to that hook, and the `Addr.hollow()` body is a never-used fallback (NOT `@innate`
### — an unrecognized `@innate` T-method is folded to a default before the rewrite runs).
### See internal-wiki/v0.4.x-cycle-collector.md §9.3.
### :returns: The address of the hook.
infallible routine T.roam_trace_ref() -> Addr
    return Addr.hollow()

### Builder intrinsic: yields a closure over this type's synthesized `roam_free` hook (tears down
### non-`Roamed` fields + frees the entity). Rewritten by ExpressionLoweringPass, `Addr.hollow()` fallback.
### :returns: The address of the hook.
infallible routine T.roam_free_ref() -> Addr
    return Addr.hollow()

### Builder intrinsic: yields this type's `destruct` as a native code address (RoamHookRefLoweringPass), the
### drop hook the last strong release runs. `Addr.hollow()` fallback.
### :returns: The address of the hook.
infallible routine T.roam_drop_ref() -> Addr
    return Addr.hollow()

### Creates a controller with one strong reference in LOCAL mode (unlocked, non-atomic).
### :param data: The address of the entity; ownership transfers to this controller.
### :param trace_hook: The entity type's `roam_trace` hook (`roam_trace_ref()`).
### :param free_hook: The entity type's `roam_free` hook (`roam_free_ref()`).
### :param drop_hook: The entity type's `destruct` (`roam_drop_ref()`).
### :returns: The resulting `RoamManager` value.
### `infallible`: nothing here can fail in a way a caller receives, and a `check` around it would wrap the new controller
### in a carrier whose teardown frees it, while the handle made from it still points at it.
infallible dangerous routine RoamManager(data: Addr, trace_hook: Addr, free_hook: Addr, drop_hook: Addr) -> RoamManager
    return RoamManager(
        count: 1,
        weak_count: 0,
        dead: Unbroken[U8](initial: 0),
        escaped: Unbroken[U8](initial: 0),
        data: data,
        locked: Unbroken[U8](initial: 0),
        holder_task: Unbroken[U64](initial: 0),
        depth: 0,
        state: RoamState.LIVE,
        buffered_at: 0,
        trace_hook: trace_hook,
        free_hook: free_hook,
        drop_hook: drop_hook,
        shape_users: 0,
        kept: Addr.hollow(),
    )

# ============================================================================
# Biased reference counting — branches on mode: non-atomic (LOCAL) vs atomic (ESCAPED). The work happens in
# Ingrid's Roamed runtime (Ingrid/lapila/roam.lpa), shared with Mielia; these methods pass it this controller.
# ============================================================================

### This controller's address, as Ingrid's Roamed routines take it (their `RoamHeader` repeats this layout).
### :returns: The address of the controller.
secret routine RoamManager.header() -> Addr
    danger
        return me.hijack().get_address()

### Adds an alias. Non-atomic in LOCAL mode (fast), atomic once ESCAPED. The count mutation is bracketed
### in the collector's SHARED stop-the-world lock so a concurrent cycle-collection pass (which trial-
### deletes counts non-atomically) can never race it. On the collector's own thread the lock is a no-op.
routine RoamManager.hold()
    danger
        C::ingrid_roam_hold(header: me.header())
    return

### Drops an alias. At zero the managed entity is destroyed immediately (deterministic teardown).
### A decrement that does NOT reach zero registers the object as a cycle-collection candidate.
### The whole decrement — count drop, the buffered/eager-free branch, and the candidate report — runs
### under the collector's SHARED stop-the-world lock, so a collection pass can neither race the count nor
### free a controller it is mid-traversal over. The entity is destroyed through `drop_hook`. On the collector's
### own thread (a finalizer release) the lock is a no-op.
routine RoamManager.unhold()
    danger
        C::ingrid_roam_unhold(header: me.header())
    return

### Makes this entity keep another one alive: one more strong handle to the controller at `kept`, let go when this
### entity's last strong handle goes. A controller it kept before is let go now.
### :param kept: The other entity's controller.
dangerous routine RoamManager.keep(kept: Addr)
    C::ingrid_roam_keep(header: me.header(), kept: kept)
    return

### Takes the entity out of this controller when one strong handle and no weak observer reach it, freeing the
### controller. Anything more leaves the entity where it is.
### :returns: The entity's address, or the none address when something else still reaches it.
dangerous routine RoamManager.release_inner() -> Addr
    return C::ingrid_roam_release_inner(header: me.header())

### Returns the current strong count. Snapshot only.
### :returns: The number of live strong handles.
routine RoamManager.strong_count() -> U64
    danger
        return C::ingrid_roam_strong_count(header: me.header())

# ============================================================================
# EXPERIMENT — object-level liveness (weak observation + tombstone). LOCAL/single-thread only.
# A weak observer keeps the CONTROLLER alive after the entity data is freed, so `is_destroyed()`
# can safely answer without dangling. `observe`/`unobserve` mirror `hold`/`unhold` for the weak count.
# ============================================================================

### Registers a weak observer (does NOT keep the entity alive; keeps the controller as a tombstone).
### Bracketed in the collector's SHARED lock and atomic once ESCAPED — mirrors `hold`, so a concurrent
### collection pass (EXCLUSIVE) can never race the weak count or free a controller mid-`cyclic_finalize`.
### SAFE PRECONDITION: only ever called through an already-kept reference (a live strong handle or another
### weak observer), so the controller is guaranteed alive at entry — no observe-races-free window.
dangerous routine RoamManager.observe()
    C::ingrid_roam_observe(header: me.header())
    return

### Drops a weak observer. When the LAST observer leaves a DEAD (tombstoned) controller, the controller
### struct is finally freed. If the entity is still alive, only the observer count drops. Bracketed +
### atomic like `unhold` (last-drop detected by the atomic-sub's previous value in ESCAPED mode).
dangerous routine RoamManager.unobserve()
    C::ingrid_roam_unobserve(header: me.header())
    return

### Whether the observed entity is still alive. Safe on a tombstone (reads the atomic `dead` flag, never
### `data`). A lock-free snapshot, like `strong_count`.
### :returns: `true` until the entity's data is freed.
routine RoamManager.is_alive() -> Bool
    danger
        return not C::ingrid_roam_is_destroyed(header: me.header())

### Whether the observed entity has been destroyed. Path-agnostic: true once the entity DATA is freed by
### the RC-drop (`unhold`) OR the cycle-collect (`cyclic_finalize`) path — NOT keyed on the strong count,
### which a cycle-collected node keeps non-zero via its internal edges.
### :returns: `true` once it is gone.
routine RoamManager.is_destroyed() -> Bool
    danger
        return C::ingrid_roam_is_destroyed(header: me.header())

# ============================================================================
# Escape — one-way LOCAL -> ESCAPED promotion.
# ============================================================================

### Flips to ESCAPED (idempotent). Runs on the owner BEFORE the handle is published to another
### thread (the builder inserts it at the escape site, pre-spawn), so no concurrent access races
### the flip. After this, `count` is atomic and the reentrant lock is live.
### Escape is a GRAPH property, not per-object: everything reachable through this object's lock is
### reachable by the crossing task too, so it must escape as well (a one-object flip would leave a LOCAL
### child — non-atomic count, no lock — that both the owner and the crossing task then touch, a data race).
### Transitive escape walks the `Roamed` children through the per-type trace hook, iteratively (a deep graph
### would overflow the stack), and stops at already-escaped nodes, so cycles terminate.
infallible dangerous routine RoamManager.promote()
    C::ingrid_roam_promote(header: me.header())
    return

### Whether this object has escaped. Drives `Roamed`'s access-lock wrapping.
### :returns: `true` if ESCAPED.
routine RoamManager.is_escaped() -> Bool
    danger
        return C::ingrid_roam_is_escaped(header: me.header())

# ============================================================================
# Reentrant, task-keyed exclusive lock — active only in ESCAPED mode.
# ============================================================================

### Mode-checked lock entry: acquires the reentrant lock only when ESCAPED (a no-op in LOCAL mode,
### where there is no contention). Drives `Roamed`'s access wrapping and the `Roaming[T]` guard token.
@inline
dangerous routine RoamManager.guard_enter()
    C::ingrid_roam_lock_enter(header: me.header())
    return

### A debug build's check once the lock is taken: every handle the entity holds must be escaped when the entity is, or
### another task would reach the handle without its lock. The check is not in a release build.
### :throws: {SharingViolationError} when an escaped entity holds a handle that has not escaped.
### :param holder: The name of the entity's type, for the message.
dangerous routine RoamManager.require_shared_handles(holder: Text)
    var unshared: Addr = C::ingrid_roam_unshared_child(header: me.header())
    if not unshared.is_hollow()
        throw SharingViolationError(holder: holder)
    return

### Mode-checked lock exit: the `guard_enter` counterpart.
@inline
dangerous routine RoamManager.guard_exit()
    C::ingrid_roam_lock_exit(header: me.header())
    return

# ============================================================================
# Teardown.
# ============================================================================

### The address of the managed entity, without keeping it alive.
### :returns: The entity's address.
routine RoamManager.data_address() -> Addr
    return me.data

### Ends the controller. The entity itself is freed by the release and cycle collection paths.
@override
routine RoamManager.destruct()
    danger
        return
